data.content:
Your `ReportGenerator` has several untestable statics beyond just file I/O. Here's the recommended approach for your .NET 10 project:

---

### 1. File System → `System.IO.Abstractions` (NuGet)

This is the battle-tested solution for `File.*` and `Directory.*`:

```
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
```

Register in DI:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

Inject into your class:
```csharp
public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    // Replace: File.WriteAllText(path, content)
    fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(path, content);

    // Replace: Directory.Exists(dir)
    fileSystem.Directory.Exists(dir);

    // Replace: Directory.CreateDirectory(dir)
    fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(dir);
}
```

For tests, install the testing helpers:
```
dotnet add <TestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers
```
```csharp
var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs);
generator.GenerateReport("sales");
Assert.True(mockFs.File.Exists("/tmp/reports/sales_20260716_204259.txt"));
```

---

### 2. `DateTime.UtcNow` → Built-in `TimeProvider`

.NET 10 has this built in — no custom wrapper needed:

```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton(TimeProvider.System);
```
```csharp
public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem, TimeProvider timeProvider)
{
    var timestamp = timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("yyyyMMdd_HHmmss");
}
```

Test with `FakeTimeProvider` (from `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing` NuGet):
```csharp
var fakeTime = new FakeTimeProvider(
    new DateTimeOffset(2026, 7, 16, 12, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));
var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs, fakeTime);
```

---

### 3. `Environment.*` → Custom `IEnvironmentProvider`

No built-in exists, so generate a minimal wrapper covering only the two calls you use:

```csharp
public interface IEnvironmentProvider
{
    string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable);
    string MachineName { get; }
}

public sealed class EnvironmentProvider : IEnvironmentProvider
{
    public string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable)
        => Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(variable);
    public string MachineName => Environment.MachineName;
}
```
```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IEnvironmentProvider, EnvironmentProvider>();
```

---

### Summary

| Static | Abstraction | Source |
|---|---|---|
| `File.*`, `Directory.*` | `IFileSystem` | `System.IO.Abstractions` NuGet |
| `DateTime.UtcNow` | `TimeProvider` | Built-in (.NET 8+) |
| `Environment.*` | `IEnvironmentProvider` | Custom wrapper (above) |
| `Console.WriteLine` | `IConsole` | Custom wrapper (if needed) |

